<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=smallpox-vaccine">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Medicine and health</p><h1 class="enc-title">Smallpox vaccine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> vaccine is the first vaccine developed against a contagious disease: in 1796 the British physician Edward Jenner showed that infection with the mild cowpox virus gave immunity to smallpox; his Inquiry of 1798 presented cowpox inoculation as a safe alternative to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/variolation">variolation</a>. The word vaccine comes from vacca, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> for cow. Passed from arm to arm and later grown on calves, the vaccine served the WHO's global campaign of 1958–1977 that eradicated smallpox, the only human disease to be eradicated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/smallpox-vaccine.jpg" alt="Smallpox vaccine" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Gillray · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_cow_pock.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1796</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Berkeley, England</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Edward Jenner · <a href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Benjamin Jesty and others had tried cowpox inoculation from 1774; Jenner was the first to publish the evidence.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/variolation">Variolation<span>16th century</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/polio-vaccine">Polio vaccine<span>1950</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=smallpox-vaccine">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
